# Calcium, showing off

Every answer below was computed by the engine. Edit anything;
everything follows.

## Units nobody asked for

The classic system administrator's velocity — one attoparsec per
microfortnight is almost exactly an inch per second:

    1 attoparsec/microfortnight in inches/s => 1.0043 inches/s

The speed of light, in MIT bridge lengths per nuclear-physics instant:

    speed of light in smoots/shake => 1.7616 smoots/shake

Swatch Internet Time was right all along — the day divides perfectly:

    1 day in beats => 1,000 beats

Grandpa Simpson's car gets forty miles to the gallon, which is to say:

    40 miles/gallon in furlongs/hogshead => 20,160 furlongs/hogshead

Noah's ark, for the modern shipyard:

    ark length = 300 cubits in m => 137.16 m

## Units you define yourself

If Helen's was the face that launched a thousand ships:

    Helen = 1000 ships
    achaean fleet = 1186 ships
    achaean fleet in Helen => 1.186 Helen

Any two things with the same dimension convert:

    giraffes = 900 kg
    blue whale = 150000 kg
    1 blue whale in giraffes => 166.6667 giraffes

## Pizza economics

Is the big one worth it? Square centimetres per dollar:

    value(d, price) = pi * (d/2)^2 / price
    value(18 inch, 24 USD) in cm^2/USD => 68.4055 cm^2/$
    value(12 inch, 14 USD) in cm^2/USD => 52.1185 cm^2/$

The big one. It is always the big one.

## It solves equations, with units on

Drop a penny from the Eiffel Tower:

    g = 9.81 m/s^2
    330 m = 1/2 * g * fall time^2
    fall time => 8.2023 s

## Llama party

    party +=
        cake = 40 USD
        balloons = 12 USD
        llama rental = 350 USD
    party => $402

    tip = 18% * party => $72.36
    total = party + tip => $474.36

## And the rest

    factorial(n) = if n <= 1 then 1 else n * factorial(n - 1)
    factorial(13) => 6,227,020,800

    (2 + 3i) * (2 - 3i) => 13

    350 degF in degC => 176.6667 degC
